# Frontend standards

- **Design doc**: For UI that displays projects, artifacts, or the game runner, follow [docs/multi-agent-game-builder-design.md](docs/multi-agent-game-builder-design.md) §3. That section is the source of truth for product UI.
- **Shell**: Left sidebar with **+ New game** and a **Games** list (`GET /api/projects`, sorted by `updatedAt`). Desk routes live under the `(desk)` group; Play stays outside the sidebar.
- **Surfaces**: `/` new game; `/projects/[id]` single project card (brief inline + stage buttons → deliverables); `/projects/[id]/play` full-bleed Phaser.
- **Copy**: Keep labels short. Do not add instructional paragraphs the layout already makes obvious.
- **Visual direction**: Whimsical retro / arcade studio — pixel display for brand/labels, readable body type, orange-cream + lavender palette, chunky panels.
- **Next.js**: Use the App Router (`app/`). Prefer Server Components by default; use Client Components (`"use client"`) for interactivity (forms, polling, sidebar). Use TypeScript with strict mode.
- **API**: Typed client under `lib/api`. Poll GET `/api/projects/:id` until terminal state; refresh the games list on navigation.
- **Phaser runner**: Isolate on `/projects/[id]/play`. Load the game bundle from the API when available.
- **Testing**: Vitest for unit tests; Playwright for E2E (new game → desk → stage deliverables → play when available).
